[1] Watch glossary. Open heart: a cut-out in the dial that shows part of the moving balance wheel.

[2] Watch glossary. Chronograph: a watch with a built-in stopwatch, operated by pushers beside the crown.

[3] Store FAQ (Batteries and power). Do automatic watches need a battery? No. They are powered by the movement of your wrist.

